 "result_text": "`checkout_github_prs()` no longer fails when no PRs match. It now prints a warning and returns without fetching or checking out anything. I haven't run any tests or tried it against GitHub.\n\nThe change is in `git_machete/client.py`. `__get_valid_pull_requests` used to raise a `MacheteException` in each of these cases. It now warns instead:\n- no PRs are open in the repository (when asking for all of them)\n- the current user has no open PRs\n- the `--by` user has no open PRs\n- none of the explicitly given PR numbers exist\n\nThe last case is a change you didn't spell out: a single missing PR number used to raise an error, and now it only warns. Say so if you'd rather keep the error for explicit numbers.",
